    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In a move that reeked of desperate comedy, the franchise executed a mid-season firing with just eight games left on the clock. Enter the last-minute ringmaster, whose improbable hot streak of seven wins and an overtime loss was the season's punchline to every doomsayer. He then led the team on a playoff circus past Utah and Anaheim, setting the stage for the final gag.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
